{
  "about": "Cases every spec runner's `values:` comparison must agree on. `cell` is a cell in TCK value notation, `actual` a result value in the neutral form below, `match` the verdict. `dialect` is `tck` where the case needs `values_dialect: tck`, otherwise `strict`. `unordered_lists` sets that flag. Neutral form: null and booleans as themselves; {\"int\": \"<digits>\"}; {\"float\": \"<text>\" or \"NaN\", \"Inf\", \"-Inf\"}; {\"string\": \"...\"}; [list]; {\"map\": {key: value}}; {\"node\": {\"id\": n, \"labels\": [...], \"properties\": {...}}}; {\"relationship\": {\"id\": n, \"type\": \"T\", \"source\": n, \"target\": n, \"properties\": {...}}}; {\"path\": {\"nodes\": [node], \"relationships\": [relationship]}}; {\"cypher\": \"<expression>\"} for the value `RETURN <expression>` gives (temporals, so their Cypher toString() is Grafeo's own). A case with `limitation` is a known false verdict, the opposite of `match`, until the engine fixes what it names: runners assert the opposite, so the fix flips it.",
