  "about_round_trips": "Each binding's own temporal fidelity: `RETURN <cypher> AS v`, then `RETURN toString($v)` with that value passed back as a parameter, must give `text`. `runner_gaps` names, per runner, the issue under which the case is a strict expected failure (it must fail there, so the fix flips it); the zone id is an engine gap, so every runner fails it. The same `runner_gaps` key on a case above works the same way."
